From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 23:00:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] R14 shadow fix: scale skylight GI fill (was ~55% of film
 mean, burying every shadow)

The kernel produced shadows correctly; they were invisible because the open
Showcase's 2pi sky dome fed escaped bounce rays ~55% of the film's mean
radiance, shrinking every key light's lit-vs-shadowed ratio to ~1.2:1 (sun,
panels, emissives, spots all suffered alike -- the user's 'no shadows anywhere').
CPU-mirror A/B (shipped kernel path, shipped denoiser): fill x1.00 film mean
0.3636 flat vs x0.25 mean 0.2141 with crisp directional shadows.

- Kernel: new push-constant float SkyFillScale (ex-PushReserve4 lane, 128-B
  block unchanged) scales ONLY the escaped bounce-ray sky collection; backdrop
  sky, sun disc and all NEE terms untouched; <0 = legacy 1.0 for old captures.
- Host: DispatchConfiguration mirrors the lane (static_assert 128 B holds);
  ReSTIRIntegrator AssignSkyFillScale (clamp [0,1], reset on change, default
  0.35); Celestial panel gains the 'Sky fill' slider (0..1) beside 'Direct';
  GameExecution assigns it per frame and logs a [Lighting] line (sun gain,
  fill, exposure mode+value, sun pick, lamp power) beside [Shadows].
- Mirror: g_SkyGiScale default 0.35 mirrors the product default; --sky-gi
  override; usage documents --sun-direct/--sun-pick/--sky-gi.

Validation: shader gate 15/15 GREEN (glslang 16.6.0 built in-sandbox);
ShaderTableParity/BuildSourceList/ShowcaseLevel/TelemetryProbe/
PerformanceTelemetry GREEN; GameExecution/CelestialSequence/ReSTIRIntegrator
g++ -fsyntax-only clean; A/B + night renders in Diagnostics/Renders.

